+# Sabooor ARRI — Fuji + Canon controls
+
+Canon EOS 600D / Canon firmware 1.0.2. Layout preserved. Experimental camera build: computer tests do not establish hardware stability or real-time performance.
+
+## Implemented
+
+- Image > Look > Look: OFF / Canon, Fuji Provia 100F, Velvia 50, Superia X-Tra 400. These are creative film-stock emulations generated using JanLohse/spectral_film_lut, not official Fujifilm camera simulations. Input assumes display-referred sRGB and ML signed-chroma BT.601; not calibrated against the Canon Picture Style pipeline. They process only the LCD preview and never the recorded H.264. HDMI LUT processing is unavailable in the native backend. Default OFF.
+- Look Intensity: 0/25/50/75/100%. Canon Picture Style remains available separately and DOES affect H.264.
+- Recording Resolution: 1920x1080, 1280x720, 640x480.
+- Project Settings > Project Rate: 1080p 23.976/29.97, 720p 59.94, 480p 29.97. PAL rates 25/50 are excluded. The selector lists 23.976, 24, 29.97, 30 and 59.94 without p suffixes. 24/30 are explicitly disclosed rounded aliases for the same native 23.976/29.97 cadences, not exact rates. Selecting 59.94 automatically selects 1280x720; selecting 23.976/24 from 720p or 480p selects 1920x1080. A success-only popup reports automatic resolution changes. Changing resolution can select a compatible cadence automatically. PAL/NTSC is never changed by Sabooor: choose the video system in Canon menu first. The selector always lists all five NTSC labels; when Canon is still in PAL, an instruction requests NTSC and no video-mode change is sent. Applying a mode closes the custom menu and queues property requests on a separate worker, outside the GUI key handler and menu lock. Changes are blocked during recording, outside movie mode, when properties have unexpected lengths, or while ML FPS override is enabled. Failed confirmation shows a notification; no automatic property rollback is attempted. Hardware confirmation is still needed.
+- Lens Squeeze Factor: existing ML anamorphic preview, LCD only, off through 2x. The monitor now runs the native display-filter stage; simultaneous Fuji LUT and anamorphic preview is supported by the host-tested renderer.
+- Frame Line: white 1.78:1, 2.35:1, 1:1 and 9:16 guides. Enable via Frame Line A / Frame Lines or VF surround mask. Guides do not crop the recording.
+- VF means the camera LCD. SDI presentation labels changed to HDMI; unsupported input/second-port controls remain N/A. Monitor Surround Mask controls the Sabooor overlay on HDMI, not the physical HDMI signal or clean-HDMI output.
+- Magnification / Master Magnification: Canon 1x, 5x, 10x LCD zoom, blocked while recording.
+- Next Reel Count: editable project counter saved in ML settings; does not rename Canon clips. Camera Index: A.
+- Erase Media: launches the Canon menu with Format-card instructions; select and confirm formatting in the Canon interface. Opening this item does NOT erase anything. No card formatting was performed by the assistant.
+- User Buttons: actual Canon button labels. Existing Canon actions remain unchanged; this does not implement arbitrary button remapping.
+- Setup and Lens & ECS actions were left unavailable as requested. Metadata has no new MOV integration. System/Power/Genlock have no added controls.
+
+REC start/stop and media-full beeps are still N/A: the upstream 600D port disables REC beeps because of possible audio interference. No dummy On/Off controls were added. Independent beeps need a separate implementation and hardware audio tests.
+
+## Installation on an already prepared card
+
+Back up autoexec.bin and ML/modules/600D_102.sym together. Copy their matching replacements and the ML/LOOKS directory from the update ZIP. Keep existing fonts, settings and DCIM. Do not run the Canon firmware updater or installer again. Use the reader with the camera powered off and eject safely. To roll back, restore the two backed-up core files together; LUT files may remain unused.
+
+## Checks and provenance
+
+Host tests execute production C for mode setters, validation, property acknowledgements, no writes to video-system settings, and deferred changes outside GUI/menu locks (Canon property I/O stubbed), LUT loader/checksum/error handling, signed-UYVY transformation, source preservation, buffer bounds, eight squeeze ratios, four frame guides, menu navigation/cancellation and existing REC overlay rules. No camera, microphone, audio recording or HDMI hardware test was performed.
+
+Each LUT is 32x32x32 in signed-YUV form, loaded dynamically (~128 KiB); preview uses the native separate display buffer (~675 KiB). Memory/file errors disable the new LUT. Native external-monitor and display-mode gates remain in place. No extra boot reservation or encoder-buffer redirection was introduced. Build must pass tools/check-600d-memory.py.
+
+Generation: use tools/make-sabooor-fuji.py with the spectral_film_lut source path on PYTHONPATH. data/sabooor/looks/manifest.json pins the upstream commit and generated hashes; its MIT notice is included. Generated .cube files are also included for inspection/post-production, with the stated sRGB approximation.
+
+Canon modes source: https://asia.canon/en/support/6200098100
+Film model: https://github.com/JanLohse/spectral_film_lut
